{title: 238 - How Sweet the Name!}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F#m]How [D/A]sweet [A]the [G]name [A]of Jesus [D/A]sounds
[D/A]In [Em/B]a believer's [D/A]ear!
[D]It soothes his [Bm]sorrows, [A/E]heals [Em]his [D]wounds,
[D/F#]And drives [Em/G]away [A7/E]his [D/F#]fear.

Verse 2:
[F#m]It makes [A]the [G]wounded [A]spirit [A7]whole,
[D/A]And [Em/B]calms the [G]troubled [D/A]breast;
[D]"Tis [G]manna [Bm]to [D]the [A/E]hungry [D]soul,
[D/F#]And to [Em/G]the [D/F#]weary, rest.

Verse 3:
[F#m]Dear [D/A]name, [A]the [G]rock [A]on which [A7]I [D/A]build,
[D/A]My [Em/B]shield and [D/A]hiding place,
[D]My neverfailing treasury, filled
[D/F#]With boundless [Em/G]stores [A7/E]of [D/F#]grace.

Verse 4:
[F#m]Jesus! [A]my [G]Shepherd, [A]Guardian, [D/A]Friend,
[D/A]My [Em/B]Prophet, [D/A]Priest, [G]and [D/A]King!
[D]My [G]Lord, [D/A]my [Bm]life, [D]my [A/E]way, [Em]my [D]end!
[D/F#]Accept [Em/G]the [D/F#]praise [A7/E]I [D/F#]bring.

Verse 5:
[F#m]Weak [D/A]is [A]the [G]effort [A]of [A7]my [D/A]heart,
[D/A]And [Em/B]cold my [D/A]warmest thought;
[D]But [G]when [D/A]I [Bm]see [D]Thee [A/E]as [Em]Thou [D]art,
[D/F#]I'll praise [Em/G]Thee [D/F#]as [A7/E]I [D/F#]ought.
